# Godot Documentation Context

When helping with this Godot project, use the official Godot Engine documentation as your primary reference.

**Documentation URL:** https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/

- Prefer Godot 4.x (stable) API and patterns: GDScript, nodes, scenes, signals, CharacterBody2D, Area2D, etc.
- For scripting: use [GDScript reference](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/tutorials/scripting/gdscript/index.html) and [Core features](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/tutorials/scripting/index.html).
- For 2D: use [2D](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/tutorials/2d/index.html) and [Physics](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/tutorials/physics/index.html) docs.
- When unsure about APIs or node behavior, assume the [Godot 4.x stable class reference](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/index.html) and docs are authoritative.

You can fetch or cite specific pages from the docs when needed to give accurate, up-to-date answers.
